# Code Quality Rules

## TypeScript
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow it, or define a proper type/interface
- Define all shared types in dedicated type files — never inline complex types in components
- Use `type` for object shapes, `interface` for extendable contracts
- Prefer explicit return types on all functions and API handlers

## React
- Prefer React Server Components — only add `"use client"` when you need state, effects, or browser APIs
- Never fetch data inside a `useEffect` — use Server Components or React Query / SWR
- Always handle loading and error states in every data-fetching component
- Avoid prop drilling more than 2 levels — use context or co-locate state

## Naming Conventions
- Components: `PascalCase` (e.g. `BookingCard.tsx`)
- Hooks: `camelCase` starting with `use` (e.g. `useAvailableSlots.ts`)
- API route files: `route.ts` inside descriptive folders
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`
- Zod schemas: suffix with `Schema` (e.g. `createEventSchema`)

## General
- No commented-out code in commits
- No `console.log` left in production code — use a `isDev` guard if needed
- Keep functions small and single-purpose — if it needs a comment to explain what it does, break it up
- Reuse — if you write the same logic twice, extract it into a util or hook
